# If a class with a class written below it still counted as one below whose prototype object only its own objects stand, `Disk.prototype instanceof Square` and `new Disk() instanceof Square` would be answered by the shape of Square alone, with false
# class Square { area(k) { return 4; } }  class Disk extends Square { area(k) { return 3; } }
# The twin of own-objects-alone-stand-below-the-prototype-object-of-a-class.ir. Below Square.prototype stands Disk.prototype, which no `new Square` has made. Below Disk.prototype stand the objects of Disk alone.
# RUN: link layouts mechanisms=all
# CHECK: layout L0
# CHECK-NOT: own-objects-below
# CHECK: layout L1 {{*}}own-objects-below

